# STEP 0.4.3 — containment wrapper + OOM/timeout/segfault smoke fixtures (§3.4/§3.5)

Grounding: §3.4 (per-candidate limits: --network=none, --memory=4g no-swap, 2GB tmpfs
/sandbox wiped per candidate, compile timeout 120s, run timeout max(10x golden,5s)),
§3.5 (process-level feasibility labels). Carried F9: wrapper reports labels only,
asserts no feasibility (leak-audit exit codes must not feed feasibility).

Architecture: host-side run_contained() launches each candidate as its own podman
container with the §3.4 limits + a wall-clock timeout, classifies the outcome, and
NEVER raises on candidate misbehaviour. A new container per candidate => fresh tmpfs
(wiped automatically). OOM via State.OOMKilled with a SIGKILL-137 fallback.

## in-container pure label tests (tests/test_containment_labels.py)
7 passed — classify() maps ok/timeout/memory_cap_kill/crash(SEGV,ABRT,BUS,FPE,ILL)/
nonzero_exit; run_timeout_s = max(10x,5s); §3.4 constants pinned (120s, 4096MB, 2048MB).

